 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-* **Precision:** The sequence of rotations and absolute values can accumulate floating-point errors. Use double precision if high accuracy is required near the surface [G].
-* **Degenerate Input:** The function is well-defined for all $p$ [S1, unofficial].
-* **Boundary:** The distance is 0 on the surface [G].
+*   **Precision:** The sequence of rotations and reflections can accumulate floating-point errors. Using `double` precision is recommended for high-quality SDFs.
+*   **Boundary Conditions:** Points exactly on the symmetry planes may experience discontinuities in the derivative if the modulo operation is not handled carefully (e.g., using `fmod` vs `remainder`).
+*   **Missing Distance Formula:** The source [S1, unofficial] does not provide the final scalar distance calculation after the folding steps. Implementers must derive the distance from the folded point to the nearest face of the fundamental domain.
 
